					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/univine" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(276792); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=276792&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606661429" alt="Univine" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=276792)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/univine" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(276792); return false;" >Univine</a></span> <span class="odate time_1455547628 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">15 Feb 2016 14:47</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2457561">
									

<blockquote>
<p>I'm a bit confused about his anomalous effect. If only those in the village can interact with him, what happens with those who don't live there? Does he just ignore them, or is it the other way around?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Since people who aren't from the village can't perceive him in the first place, they can't interact with him at all.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>I also don't get why you often referred to him by his blacked out name most of the time instead of his SCP designation.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The first interview took place before the anomaly was given a designation. In the third interview, the designation wasn't used because the SCP was cooperative and Dr. Wang wanted to establish a friendly, conversational tone for the interview. Also, as people have pointed out to me in the past, there's also no particular need to reveal operational information (SCP designations) to SCPs or D-Classes.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>I don't really get the sudden change in tone here. Is it because he copies the worldview of those in the village? That would make sense, but I'd still like to know.</p>
</blockquote>
<p><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anti-Japanese_sentiment_in_China">Anti-Japanese sentiment</a> is a pretty big deal in China. Also, considering that SCP-2788 saw hundreds of the people he was supposed to protect be murdered by the Japanese, it would surprise me if he <em>wasn't</em> angry at them.</p>

							</div>

								
